  "scope": "Independent review of the actual browser speed/physics frame boundary and Root smoothGraphics integration. This reviewer authored the new frame/player tests. Real-render persistent memory/RNG coupling is covered by separately attributed peer evidence, not inferred from pure drawing callbacks.",
  "checks": [
    "Player installs smoothGraphics only in createOriginalRenderer sharedOptions. state.options keeps exact captured trig, native engine callbacks and the original getTickCount provider. graphics=exact opts out; the normal query enables drawing only.",
    "Each racing paint executes one advanceFrame prefix before composeRaceFrame. The original ordered wind/AI/steering/boat-dynamics callbacks and one unpaused integratePositions call are preserved. Native odd/even paint phases remain explicit and no additional physics steps are added for faster graphics.",
    "Real integration derives dt from the original course/boat constants and speed divisor, not elapsed wall-clock drawing time. Speed10 retains divisor76 and dt0.20384122874775878 in the default course. Source tests compare all memory bytes and RNG after each frame across six real menu-selected speeds.",
    "The actual scheduler yields through one pending immediate task, applies inter-frame input before the next physics prefix, and retains original30/60/80ms remainder delays. Hidden/modal/frozen/terminal behavior remains covered by the existing source scheduler tests. Different drawing duration does not create catch-up or retries.",
    "Paused draws keep the original wind/AI/dynamics prefix while suppressing integration. A drawing failure occurs after exactly one completed numerical prefix and does not run finishFrame or retry physics.",
    "The full edition mode word0x4da16c remains0. Both graphics queries pass original fleet/tutorial/start/persistence controls and two real paints beyond the explicitly prepared clock261.5 input; no demo flag or edition mode is patched by those checks.",
    "The final standalone export passes119 browser menu/render/input checks and7 full-mode checks. Its default smooth query uses the same frozen84-file source graph; all138 generated manifest entries verify before/end and no graph drift occurs."
  ],
