  "validationLimits": [
    "Input parity is at the same simulation-frame boundary. Higher native paint throughput advances more simulation per wall second, so the same wall-time input can occur at a different race clock. No interpolation or wall-time physics loop is introduced.",
    "Pure drawing callbacks cannot prove real-render persistent-store/RNG isolation; that is why the separate render-to-engine trace evidence and exact waypoint/camera boundaries are required.",
    "Source general119 passed while one dependency guard was tightened, and source full-mode checks preceded the final before-unbox hook-order correction. The final standalone119/full-mode7 checks passed against all three guards and the corrected hooks; all84 source files and138 manifest entries stayed unchanged across that sequence.",
    "The beyond260 full-mode test uses an explicitly declared finite clock input, rather than claiming an uninterrupted race naturally reached that time. Performance/display smoothness is measured separately by Root."
  ],
